From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:10:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: tell whether a Type-C port runs DP
 Alt Mode

The display fabric routes a DP Alt Mode display through the port's DP
PHY. On T8132 that PHY runs DisplayPort on its four lanes only with its
calibration (atcphy_t8132_dp_lanes()), which the boot loader may or may
not have published, so the fabric needs to ask before it selects the
crossbar's DP PHY output.

Export apple_atc_dp_alt_lanes() next to the DP tunnel calls, found with
symbol_get() as they are: 1 or 0 for a T8132 PHY, 1 for the other
generations, whose mux decides on its own, -EINVAL for a phy that is no
ATC DP PHY. The calibration it reads is set at probe, before the phy
provider registers, and never changes, so it takes no lock.

[j604: X2-01 C2a (BOARD-SWEEP-1838 row X2). Consumer: drm C2b.]

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index 1431d6015a..bff097bd1c 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -5189,6 +5189,20 @@ int apple_atc_dp_tunnel_open(struct phy *phy)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_atc_dp_tunnel_open);
 
+/* The calibration read here is set at probe, before the provider registers. */
+int apple_atc_dp_alt_lanes(struct phy *phy)
+{
+	struct apple_atcphy *atcphy;
+
+	if (!phy || phy->ops != &apple_atc_dp_phy_ops)
+		return -EINVAL;
+	atcphy = phy_get_drvdata(phy);
+	if (atcphy->hw->gen != ATCPHY_GENERATION_T8132)
+		return 1;
+	return atcphy_t8132_dp_lanes(atcphy);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_atc_dp_alt_lanes);
+
 static struct phy *atcphy_xlate(struct device *dev, const struct of_phandle_args *args)
 {
 	struct apple_atcphy *atcphy = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-- 
